"""In-place foreach minimum (aten::_foreach_minimum_).

``self[i] <- minimum(self[i], other[i])`` with torch.minimum semantics
(NaN propagates from either operand).  Every tensor in ``self`` keeps its
storage, strides and data_ptr; the call returns ``None``.

Supported call forms (same dispatch as the ATen overloads):
  * List      : other is a Sequence[Tensor]      (primary bound contract)
  * Scalar    : other is a Python/ATen scalar
  * ScalarList: other is a Sequence[Scalar]

All elementwise work happens in Triton kernels.  A pair is executed by the
"linear" kernel when a common iteration order exists in which both operands
advance with unit stride (this covers contiguous tensors and, after
reordering/collapsing, plain transposed views).  Everything else (gaps,
broadcast, general strides) uses the rank-unrolled strided kernel.
"""

import torch
import triton
import triton.language as tl

_MAX_GROUP = 4  # tensor pairs fused into one launch
_MAX_RANK = 8  # compile-time unrolled strided rank
_MAX_GRID = 65535  # launch grid cap (API limit, not a device property)


